This talk demystifies on-device AI for Kotlin developers. We cover different models, quantization strategies, and Kotlin-friendly inference pipelines using coroutines. You’ll learn how to build features like summarization, classification, personalization, and intent extraction without needing a server.','{"id": "d9e24b425ce04b5f890eb314c6d3fcd5", "room": "Room 5, Lightning talks", "title": "Tiny Models, Big Impact: On-Device AI for Real Apps", "endsAt": 1779352200000, "category": "[Lightning talk, Intermediate, Android, AI]", "dayIndex": 1, "speakers": "[Hammad Akram]", "startsAt": 1779351300000, "phaseOfDay": "MORNING", "conferenceDay": "2026-05-21", "durationMinutes": 15, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-05-21T10:30:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-05-21T10:15:00"}'),
