75263977,0.0027198792,-0.0079422,-0.009643555,-0.0066452026,0.014625549,-0.022338867,0.016815186,-0.0005106926,-0.020126343,-0.002166748,0.030914307,0.032165527,0.01914978,0.0010070801,0.00041103363,-0.0010528564,-0.023254395,-0.024963379,-0.0039596558,0.002313614,0.03503418,0.034820557,-0.00096559525,0.014007568,-0.01625061,-0.020584106,0.025619507,0.017364502,-0.067871094,0.015174866,-0.013206482,0.043304443,0.0065460205,0.029312134,-0.0440979,0.025985718,-0.015594482,-0.013931274,0.026000977,-0.0053138733,0.028289795,0.02532959,-0.013877869,0.014533997,0.019317627,-0.030426025,0.0013494492,0.0033435822,0.0124053955,0.0049362183,0.019317627,-0.002937317,0.014434814,0.011688232,0.040802002,-0.0071907043,-0.01071167,-0.012832642,-0.03643799,0.037963867,-0.004589081,0.02607727,0.021377563,0.009811401,-0.02482605,0.00049829483,-0.011795044,0.01348114,-0.016494751,-0.0004892349,-0.007762909,0.039215088,0.0042762756,-0.009178162,0.011871338,-0.0047721863,-0.010314941,-0.022354126,-0.0113220215,0.032165527,-0.015731812,0.009460449,0.017333984,-0.004688263,0.022064209,0.012260437,-0.024169922,-0.019714355,0.03878784,-0.017105103,-0.010025024,0.0071144104,0.0022773743,0.029327393,-0.027267456,-0.004016876,0.01234436,0.0045204163,0.012413025,0.029190063,-0.0068130493,0.01234436,-0.01058197,-0.019836426,-0.028457642]'::public.vector,'title:Bringing Native iOS Feel to Compose Multiplatform Apps, description:Ever built a Compose Multiplatform app and wished it looked at home on every platform? This lightning talk introduces Calf (Compose Adaptive Look & Feel) an open-source library that makes your Compose UI adapt to each platform’s native design. We’ll start with a typical Material3 styled Android app and ask: can it feel native on iOS without a complete rewrite?

We’ll gradually replace Material components with Calf’s adaptive UI components (dialogs, bottom sheets, pickers, etc.). With just a few swaps, watch the app instantly adopt iOS’s familiar look while using the same codebase for both Android and iOS. You’ll see how Calf maps components to their native counterparts, Material on Android and Cupertino on iOS, so the UI truly feels native to each platform.

This talk is light, fast-paced, and inspirational. If you’re an Android developer curious about Kotlin Multiplatform, come see how a single Compose codebase can deliver beautiful, platform-native UIs with minimal effort.','{"id": "43d33ea24f0e447e833d6a8cce7ae4e4", "room": "Room 5, Lightning talks", "title": "Bringing Native iOS Feel to Compose Multiplatform Apps", "endsAt": 1779357600000, "category": "[Lightning talk, Introductory and overview, Multiplatform]", "dayIndex": 1, "speakers": "[Mohamed Ben Rejeb]", "startsAt": 1779356700000, "phaseOfDay": "MORNING", "conferenceDay": "2026-05-21", "durationMinutes": 15, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-05-21T12:00:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-05-21T11:45:00"}'),
