logic in Kotlin. Follow as we explore how we’ve instrumented coroutines to collect latency signals and surface usable critical paths with slack/drag support, removed sharp edges of coroutines, surfaced streams as Flows, and avoided common pitfalls. See mistakes we’ve made along the way and how we’ve fueled a revolution in server development by simplifying “asynchronous by default”.','{"id": "55c854e85ff643929d76199e0c1fcf88", "room": "Auditorium, Room 1", "title": "How google.com/search builds on Kotlin coroutines for highly scalable, streaming, concurrent servers", "endsAt": 1779363900000, "category": "[Regular session, Intermediate, Server-side]", "dayIndex": 1, "speakers": "[Sam Berlin, Alessio Della Motta]", "startsAt": 1779361200000, "phaseOfDay": "AFTERNOON", "conferenceDay": "2026-05-21", "durationMinutes": 45, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-05-21T13:45:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-05-21T13:00:00"}'),
