In this fun, dialogue-style session, mobile performance experts and newly minted co-founders Lauren Darcey and Eric Kuck explore the eternal tension between "making it delightful" and "making it performant."

What happens when mobile performance-focused developers lean in to building some of the most intensive user experiences, from particle effects to shared element transitions, and push the limits of what to expect from mobile devices with KMP and CMP?

In 2026, the bar for app quality has never been higher. We move beyond simple "moments of delight" to architect apps where whimsy is the core feature, not just a decoration. We dig into the heavy lifting required to support this vision: the specific animation frameworks, asset pipelines, and multimedia choices needed to drive next-gen UX without killing the battery or grinding the device frame rates to a halt.

This is a candid look at the architectural and performance tradeoffs facing developers today with KMP and CMP. We demonstrate how Compose Multiplatform allows us to bridge the gap between high-impact design and hardcore engineering constraints in ways we never could before.

You’ll leave with new ideas on how to incorporate foundational performance posture into your apps, and more confidence in using the powerful cross-platform frameworks and device features to their fullest potential.','{"id": "dc81de99829f47d29804df0b6addf228", "room": "Room 13b", "title": "Adventures in Whimsical UX: The Tug-of-War Between Delight & Performance", "endsAt": 1779458400000, "category": "[Regular session, Intermediate, Multiplatform, Android, Extensibility/Tooling, Language and best practices, Other]", "dayIndex": 2, "speakers": "[Lauren Darcey, Eric Kuck]", "startsAt": 1779455700000, "phaseOfDay": "AFTERNOON", "conferenceDay": "2026-05-22", "durationMinutes": 45, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-05-22T16:00:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-05-22T15:15:00"}'),
