714157,-0.029815674,-0.00020337105,0.0038986206,-0.009666443,-0.0042533875,0.041046143,0.00030374527,-0.027252197,-0.0030727386,0.023452759,0.04989624,0.0019512177,-0.009269714,0.0073432922,0.025772095,0.0039978027,-0.040496826,-0.0002682209,0.02658081,-0.01701355,0.03463745,0.010269165,-0.0009860992,-0.0009460449,-0.007701874,0.012649536,0.010734558,-0.06616211,-0.0069122314,-0.009918213,0.008300781,0.0058670044,-0.026901245,-0.008583069,0.03765869,0.0027389526,0.013893127,0.015426636,0.008880615,0.026916504,-0.031219482,6.0737133e-05,0.0060768127,0.029418945,0.0016393661,0.01235199,0.01473999,0.008018494,-0.0127334595,0.04095459,-0.017120361,-0.0209198,-0.018066406,0.030975342,-0.022384644,-0.012268066,0.01626587,-0.0035190582,-0.005264282,-0.028747559,0.013710022,0.022323608,0.0066223145,-0.0074043274,0.011123657,0.016326904,0.010871887,-0.012702942,0.0013408661,-0.016677856,0.023452759,0.0206604,-0.01675415,-0.022598267,0.004119873,-0.011795044,-0.027114868,-0.011291504,0.005207062,-0.02998352,-0.016677856,0.010154724,-0.024795532,0.017913818,-0.0031051636,0.0019836426,-0.015899658,-0.00472641,-0.023010254,-0.016174316,0.0020923615,0.0052986145,-0.007858276,-0.023925781,-0.035339355,0.046539307,-0.007446289,0.03213501,0.02571106,-0.03012085,0.0040779114,-0.010520935,-0.023544312,-0.027236938]'::public.vector,'title:Kotlin Analysis API in Practice: Semantic Smarts for Code Migrations, description:Code migrations are tedious: you need to rewrite syntax while preserving behavior, and one wrong assumption can break downstream consumers. PSI helps locate and transform code, but it can''t answer the semantic questions that determine whether a transformation is actually safe.

Kotlin Analysis API fills that gap. We''ll show how we leverage its semantic capabilities—types, symbols, call-site resolution, and diagnostics—to validate intent before we rewrite. This lets us tighten visibilities without breaking consumers, simplify nullability only when every code path stays safe, and confidently transform framework patterns.

We''ll walk through real examples showing how to query types, resolve symbols, inspect visibility, and leverage diagnostics—the building blocks for safer automated rewrites.

Using Uber''s Java-to-Kotlin migration as our running example, attendees will leave with a practical blueprint for combining PSI''s syntactic power with Kotlin Analysis API''s semantic insight—patterns that apply to any large-scale code transformation.','{"id": "71694362c1054eb2ad9e5ce2a54687ea", "room": "Room 5, Lightning talks", "title": "Kotlin Analysis API in Practice: Semantic Smarts for Code Migrations", "endsAt": 1779362100000, "category": "[Lightning talk, Intermediate, Extensibility/Tooling]", "dayIndex": 1, "speakers": "[Idan Nakav]", "startsAt": 1779361200000, "phaseOfDay": "AFTERNOON", "conferenceDay": "2026-05-21", "durationMinutes": 15, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-05-21T13:15:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-05-21T13:00:00"}');
