0.019592285,-0.03125,-0.0025634766,0.017440796,-0.0066947937,-0.020263672,0.033721924,-0.002368927,-0.02230835,0.0004324913,0.042633057,0.040374756,-0.005012512,-0.008422852,-0.010696411,0.014060974,-0.00042247772,-0.010551453,-0.00044965744,0.0023860931,-0.004917145,0.012832642,0.0029907227,0.018203735,-0.038330078,-0.0013513565,0.0132751465,0.0014734268,-0.051452637,0.009140015,-0.002445221,0.01739502,0.010559082,0.008087158,-0.028686523,0.054534912,0.011550903,0.013053894,0.012161255,0.0028419495,0.06365967,0.0259552,0.006580353,0.014335632,0.008522034,-0.044525146,0.015174866,0.0063705444,0.0076522827,0.004337311,0.035461426,0.011764526,0.006832123,-0.001917839,0.026535034,-0.0034885406,-0.008796692,-0.016326904,0.0039482117,-0.0018062592,-0.051513672,0.025817871,-0.0053596497,0.011299133,-0.0209198,0.0287323,-0.0046081543,0.0022888184,-0.033447266,0.040283203,-0.01008606,-0.003370285,0.0052108765,-0.0069122314,0.0016670227,0.0006799698,0.006706238,-0.018188477,-0.0073127747,0.0035896301,-0.024841309,-0.0009202957,0.013946533,-0.028747559,0.027114868,0.0154953,-0.014312744,-0.034851074,-0.00040459633,0.014701843,-0.033325195,0.008712769,0.0015029907,0.010253906,-0.03353882,-0.034088135,0.028778076,0.0013370514,0.02444458,0.02482605,-0.028259277,0.0062675476,-0.03265381,-0.013381958,-0.034088135]'::public.vector,'title:Concurrency Patterns for Modern High Performance Kotlin Servers, description:Kotlin Coroutines revolutionized asynchronous programming, but mastering them for high-performance server applications requires more than just launch and async. This session dives deep into battle-tested concurrency patterns, the reusable, structured solutions, that underpin fast, scalable Kotlin servers, particularly the ones making many RPC calls.

We will break down complex server problems into distinct concurrency challenges and show how Kotlin''s rich async primitives provide elegant, structured answers. You will learn practical techniques for managing server-side RPC traffic:

1. Unary RPC Patterns:
Implementing robust features like efficient request Generator flows, optimizing resource usage with Fan-in techniques, and ensuring reliability through structured Timing out and Request Hedging.

2. Streaming RPC Patterns:
Tackling the complexity of continuous data streams, from preventing memory overloads with effective Back-pressure handling and intelligent Buffering to maximizing throughput using concurrent Mapping & Merging. We will also explore advanced concepts like Reordering for improved client-side responsiveness.

By the end of this session, you won''t just understand how to use Coroutines; you''ll understand how to compose them into powerful, production-ready concurrency patterns, exemplified by a live demo of building a pretty complex Google search clone. Equip yourself with the patterns necessary to build your next high-performance, concurrent Kotlin services.','{"id": "4bbebf111a884e2eb39ae1e4e8bc939e", "room": "Auditorium, Room 1", "title": "Concurrency Patterns for Modern High Performance Kotlin Servers", "endsAt": 1779367500000, "category": "[Regular session, Intermediate, Server-side, Language and best practices]", "dayIndex": 1, "speakers": "[Bowen Feng]", "startsAt": 1779364800000, "phaseOfDay": "AFTERNOON", "conferenceDay": "2026-05-21", "durationMinutes": 45, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-05-21T14:45:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-05-21T14:00:00"}'),
