In this session, we will talk about the initiatives and resources of the Kotlin Foundation Education Committee for educators and students.

We’ll also explore how education is changing and how we are adapting. We’ll discuss approaches to:
- Teaching students to build multiplatform apps with Kotlin.
- Integrating AI tools into the learning and teaching process.
- Improving the quality of AI-generated Kotlin code and guiding students to use AI responsibly.

This session combines presentations with an extended Q&A and discussion segment. We’ll also ask you to provide feedback on what resources and priorities are most valuable for you in teaching Kotlin.

Join us for an interactive session to talk about how we can better support you!','{"id": "5cf172800679411684e69ca55ed1f4cd", "room": "Room 3", "title": "Interactive Session on Kotlin Education", "endsAt": 1779372000000, "category": "[Discussion, Introductory and overview, Other, Education]", "dayIndex": 1, "speakers": "[Ksenia Shneyveys]", "startsAt": 1779369300000, "phaseOfDay": "AFTERNOON", "conferenceDay": "2026-05-21", "durationMinutes": 45, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-05-21T16:00:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-05-21T15:15:00"}'),
