This talk explores common challenges in AI-generated code, shares best practices for evaluation and refinement, and highlights tools and techniques that help developers ensure reliability, readability, and maintainability in Kotlin projects powered by AI.

Note: this talk was submitted in November 2025, 6 months ahead of the conference. While the principles we will talk about would likely be still relevant most likely we will be talking the newest generation of models available in Spring 2026.
