2,0.0009236336,-0.029296875,-0.031982422,-0.02067566,0.0002887249,-0.03086853,-0.031158447,0.023620605,-0.007926941,-0.017440796,-0.0031204224,0.00705719,0.0692749,0.03945923,-0.023101807,0.010795593,-0.0049591064,0.018234253,-0.015174866,-0.026931763,-0.0021820068,-0.0071258545,0.057006836,0.004348755,-0.013374329,0.0022468567,-0.020599365,0.026260376,0.007286072,-0.050048828,0.009292603,-0.012260437,-0.00970459,0.03982544,-0.008888245,-0.047851562,0.031341553,-0.0069122314,0.003326416,0.018203735,0.0039634705,0.013870239,-0.018417358,-0.006378174,-0.016143799,0.020355225,-0.026687622,0.015129089,0.010475159,0.000685215,-0.006793976,0.027023315,9.268522e-05,0.0068588257,-0.016311646,0.00944519,-0.018661499,-0.010795593,-0.004257202,0.020050049,-0.0048980713,-0.046020508,0.03366089,-0.009315491,0.0070495605,-0.004928589,0.039276123,-0.0066719055,0.012466431,-0.02331543,0.0020370483,-0.01121521,0.020889282,0.0020618439,0.00029230118,-0.003742218,0.015579224,-0.009536743,-0.011650085,-0.012382507,0.013504028,-0.041534424,0.009544373,0.0021762848,-0.037994385,0.033111572,-0.017929077,-0.006061554,-0.033447266,0.0027980804,-0.015823364,-0.028305054,-0.013793945,-0.0016288757,0.0060272217,-0.025512695,-0.034057617,0.04095459,-0.011138916,0.0073509216,0.027908325,0.015808105,-0.0029964447,-0.025817871,-0.00932312,-0.04559326]'::public.vector,'title:Beer, Fries, and the Surprisingly Easy Kotlin Meetups, description:Belgium has three languages, scattered developer communities, and a Kotlin user group (BEKUG) that went quiet after COVID. At KotlinConf two years ago we connected by chance. That sent us home motivated and energised to revive things, but we quickly hit the classic wall: no speakers, no momentum.
We decided to try OpenSpace: no CFP, no pressure, attendees build the agenda themselves on the day. One person told us afterward: "I was skeptical, but it was really fun." That was enough.
Three meetups in, we''re still learning: how to make the format feel inviting, how to balance talking with listening. But every session has organically produced community-driven conversation, and people keep coming back.
You don''t need a perfect lineup. You just need to keep showing up.
Takeaways: what OpenSpace is, how to run it for a meetup, and why organizing is worth it even when it feels hard.','{"id": "0723916db9c84e70884cd706317c7dcf", "room": "Room 3", "title": "Beer, Fries, and the Surprisingly Easy Kotlin Meetups", "endsAt": 1779375600000, "category": "[Regular session, Introductory and overview, Other, Community]", "dayIndex": 1, "speakers": "[Tim Schraepen, Simon Vergauwen]", "startsAt": 1779372900000, "phaseOfDay": "AFTERNOON", "conferenceDay": "2026-05-21", "durationMinutes": 45, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-05-21T17:00:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-05-21T16:15:00"}'),
