59033,-0.0345459,0.0070114136,0.023468018,-0.035003662,0.016525269,-0.0051193237,-0.0045051575,0.003982544,0.020812988,0.0335083,-0.0037384033,0.005619049,0.026290894,-0.00497818,-0.011016846,0.002544403,-0.0005788803,0.0009331703,0.016738892,0.028060913,0.0056381226,0.011146545,0.0027999878,-0.013061523,0.0209198,-0.0073013306,-0.06262207,0.016448975,-0.008163452,0.039367676,0.012908936,-0.022094727,-0.032470703,0.043395996,0.0064849854,0.009414673,0.015930176,0.0011453629,0.04522705,0.008888245,-0.013267517,-0.0006093979,0.01864624,-0.019851685,0.013725281,-0.010688782,0.023757935,-0.022384644,0.019470215,-0.017059326,0.025787354,0.024536133,0.021148682,-0.0079193115,-0.008331299,-0.0020656586,-0.014633179,0.014640808,-0.020324707,0.029464722,-0.008460999,0.0041885376,-0.011016846,0.009010315,0.008201599,0.020462036,0.002117157,0.010513306,-0.013755798,-0.00049734116,-0.009498596,-0.010292053,0.023849487,-0.002035141,0.0049476624,-0.022598267,0.007369995,-0.000313282,0.003534317,-0.00932312,0.013801575,-0.0037212372,0.035888672,-0.0027103424,-0.019332886,-0.005558014,0.029937744,0.011116028,-0.029830933,-0.01676941,-0.015625,0.005718231,-0.021026611,-0.013122559,0.027114868,-0.0098724365,0.006134033,0.04269409,0.00409317,-0.006641388,-0.013160706,0.0034923553,-0.019683838]'::public.vector,'title:Engineering High-Performance Multiplatform Graphic Rendering with Jetpack Compose, description:Standard animation libraries often force a compromise. GIFs consume bandwidth, Lottie struggles with complex rasters, and video formats lack frame-perfect alpha transparency. Furthermore, replicating complex text effects using these vector or raster formats is inefficient and bloated and can result in glyph shaping issues in different languages.

To drive user engagement and measurable business impact, we need tools that are easy to deploy and cost effective to maintain. In this talk, we''ll cover two explorations: a custom high-fidelity animated image sequence engine for complex visuals, and TextWave—a specialized engine for animating glyphs that offers superior efficiency and control over binary size compared to standard alternatives.

Coordinating these components to run at high FPS across 3 platforms is a massive engineering challenge. Does each platform implement it natively, or is there room for a multiplatform implementation?

In this session, we will share the architecture of building these advanced rendering engines in both native and multiplatform scenarios. We will move beyond basic UI to discuss:
* Rendering the custom graphics on each platform natively.
* Rendering the custom graphics on each platform with Compose multiplatform with Skia including working with the Kotlin Native memory model and hardware bitmaps including before-and-after profiler analysis.
* The Rendering Pipeline: How we architected a decoding pipeline that manages byte[] ownership to prevent copies and massive memory pressure—specifically addressing the "heap growth" challenges in Kotlin Native when loading compressed assets.
* Coordinating text animations with raster sequences, and the measurable impact this performance boost had on bookings.
* Interesting nuances of byte array management accross JS,  Java, and Native environments.

Join us for a deep technical dive into the state of cross-platform graphics, featuring real-world benchmarks, profiler screenshots, and the lessons learned from rendering pixels at scale.','{"id": "8851f8cd276445c8acb6a018eaa4bb74", "room": "Room 13b", "title": "Engineering High-Performance Multiplatform Graphic Rendering with Jetpack Compose", "endsAt": 1779379200000, "category": "[Regular session, Advanced, Multiplatform, Android]", "dayIndex": 1, "speakers": "[Tunji Dahunsi, Rahul Behera]", "startsAt": 1779376500000, "phaseOfDay": "AFTERNOON", "conferenceDay": "2026-05-21", "durationMinutes": 45, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-05-21T18:00:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-05-21T17:15:00"}'),
