OpenRewrite works by applying "recipes" to the Lossless Semantic Trees (LSTs) that represent your source code. The LSTs capture full type attribution and formatting, allowing for accurate, automated refactoring that respects the original coding style. ','{"id": "30720bc6a5ea4eb5931afe02ed41959e", "room": "Auditorium, Room 1", "title": "Automate upgrading to Kotlin 2 with OpenRewrite", "endsAt": 1779440400000, "category": "[Regular session, Intermediate, Extensibility/Tooling, AI]", "dayIndex": 2, "speakers": "[Rooz SF, Jonathan Schneider]", "startsAt": 1779437700000, "phaseOfDay": "MORNING", "conferenceDay": "2026-05-22", "durationMinutes": 45, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-05-22T11:00:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-05-22T10:15:00"}'),
