In 15 minutes, you’ll learn how to structure your builds, manage dependencies safely, write maintainable build logic, avoid configuration pitfalls, and speed up your CI pipelines; all with small, incremental improvements that make a big difference.

And as a bonus, you’ll get a sneak peek at real-time code inspection and best-practice fixes in IntelliJ IDEA.

Whether you build Android apps, backend services, or multiplatform libraries, you’ll walk away with a checklist you can apply immediately to make your Gradle builds faster, clearer, more reliable, and easier for your whole team to maintain.','{"id": "55e0b40d06424d2b8b7b8c6127d88690", "room": "Room 5, Lightning talks", "title": "10 Gradle Best Practices Every Kotlin Developer Should Know", "endsAt": 1779438600000, "category": "[Lightning talk, Introductory and overview, Language and best practices]", "dayIndex": 2, "speakers": "[Stefan Wolf]", "startsAt": 1779437700000, "phaseOfDay": "MORNING", "conferenceDay": "2026-05-22", "durationMinutes": 15, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-05-22T10:30:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-05-22T10:15:00"}'),
