3620605,-0.0006585121,-0.024017334,0.027526855,-0.012283325,-0.016418457,-0.011993408,0.016815186,0.033477783,0.0013122559,0.010414124,-0.034576416,0.004623413,-0.008140564,-0.019226074,-0.0034675598,0.016311646,0.0071754456,0.015808105,0.009529114,-0.00819397,-0.033050537,-0.028625488,0.009902954,0.017120361,-0.058502197,0.008415222,-0.016159058,0.023910522,0.016403198,0.01725769,-0.023544312,0.037750244,-0.015541077,-0.0068359375,-0.0023918152,0.0048294067,0.020050049,-0.012390137,0.0093307495,0.039886475,0.020812988,0.008712769,0.00705719,-0.011268616,0.021972656,-0.014053345,0.0124435425,-0.0074386597,0.027236938,0.0021858215,0.043884277,-0.014160156,-0.009262085,-0.007843018,-0.0005168915,0.00774765,-0.015777588,0.037017822,-0.005077362,-0.0054740906,-0.033599854,0.028030396,0.0014238358,-0.010383606,-0.009407043,0.012458801,0.00674057,0.024368286,0.008850098,-0.003955841,0.009895325,0.011001587,0.026000977,-0.011711121,0.018051147,0.01713562,-0.021347046,-0.003566742,0.0043792725,-0.034179688,0.023788452,-0.023086548,-0.01335907,0.0026817322,0.005218506,-0.01727295,-0.01096344,-0.014503479,0.006034851,-0.006450653,-0.004135132,-0.022567749,0.032958984,-0.026885986,-0.0073242188,0.016296387,-0.015701294,-0.012886047,-0.041229248,-0.0066833496,-0.033325195]'::public.vector,'title:Hot-Reloading Kotlin/Native, description:"Compose Hot-Reload is impossible on iOS Simulators without a JVM." If you''ve heard this, prepare to be surprised.

We will explore the experimental engineering journey of bringing hot-reload to Kotlin/Native on iOS. We’ll uncover why traditional hot-reload approaches fail on Apple’s Darwin platforms and how we bypassed these strict limitations without building a custom Kotlin Virtual Machine. Instead, you''ll see how we leveraged LLVM ORC v2 to enable hot-reload directly on iOS.

We will dive into the under-the-hood compiler changes, from split compilation to the new hot-reload runtime module, and discuss the real-world complexities of state preservation, function updates and class layout changes.

Whether you build KMP apps or love low-level runtime manipulation, you''ll leave with a glimpse into the future of the Kotlin Multiplatform developer experience.','{"id": "186d5277373a4ca5afd651b4188f37b7", "room": "Room 5, Lightning talks", "title": "Hot-Reloading Kotlin/Native", "endsAt": 1779450300000, "category": "[Lightning talk, Intermediate, Multiplatform, Extensibility/Tooling, Language and best practices]", "dayIndex": 2, "speakers": "[Gabriele Pappalardo]", "startsAt": 1779449400000, "phaseOfDay": "AFTERNOON", "conferenceDay": "2026-05-22", "durationMinutes": 15, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-05-22T13:45:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-05-22T13:30:00"}'),
