This talk describes some of the most important details from the context parameter design that library authors should take into account. We then describe the "spotlight principle" as a general guide on the context parameter / extension conundrum, and see how the general guidance applies in a few common scenarios.','{"id": "e466b9cb87d44604a6634b44e623cb33", "room": "Keynote, Room 14", "title": "Context parameters and API design", "endsAt": 1779453900000, "category": "[Regular session, Intermediate, Language and best practices]", "dayIndex": 2, "speakers": "[Alejandro Serrano Mena]", "startsAt": 1779451200000, "phaseOfDay": "AFTERNOON", "conferenceDay": "2026-05-22", "durationMinutes": 45, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-05-22T14:45:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-05-22T14:00:00"}'),
