018494,-0.011688232,-0.007003784,-0.015945435,-0.061431885,-0.04940796,0.023468018,0.0045776367,-0.018005371,0.018112183,0.005821228,0.010314941,0.018173218,0.007949829,0.05380249,0.00091314316,-0.0030841827,-0.0004310608,0.015220642,0.007843018,-0.024093628,0.0056648254,0.0024490356,-0.0057640076,0.0446167,-0.00907135,-0.0053100586,-0.025848389,-0.019577026,0.021057129,0.017868042,-0.040374756,0.009849548,-0.0008506775,-0.011009216,0.012229919,-0.03201294,-0.019989014,0.033081055,0.004688263,0.018203735,0.021026611,-0.0005335808,0.042388916,-0.013191223,-0.01828003,-0.0017948151,0.0256958,-0.004459381,0.02230835,0.014678955,0.0039367676,-0.008979797,0.027297974,-0.004108429,0.000849247,-0.015075684,0.023269653,-0.004135132,-0.03137207,0.0029716492,-0.009727478,0.01687622,-0.024215698,0.027557373,0.014915466,0.012924194,-0.0026741028,0.033111572,0.0028533936,0.019332886,-0.010154724,0.022491455,-0.016189575,0.014007568,0.018173218,-0.017318726,-0.0035057068,0.0004043579,-0.028076172,-0.009590149,-0.023422241,0.009918213,-0.016784668,0.010826111,0.0051078796,-0.017700195,0.0032997131,-0.031555176,-0.029754639,-0.015777588,0.0107803345,-0.011833191,-0.029724121,0.0029640198,-0.011367798,0.0116119385,-0.02999878,-0.019714355,0.045532227,-0.038024902,-0.0053253174,0.03564453,0.0041542053,-0.022079468,-0.019592285,-0.006340027,-0.032165527]'::public.vector,'title:Teaching Kotlin for the AI Era: Tips, Tools, and Practical Insights, description:AI is not only transforming software development but also redefining how we teach programming. As this landscape evolves, programming courses must adapt to meet new industry demands. Traditional methods, like teaching basic syntax or relying heavily on lectures, are no longer enough. Instead, we need to rethink both what we teach and how we teach, equipping students with skills relevant to an AI-driven world.

In this talk, we will share industry insights on how AI is already shaping the software development world, connect these trends to programming education, and explore how universities are integrating this into their programming courses. We’ll highlight how all of this maps to Kotlin, helping you design a Kotlin course that aligns with the rapidly evolving industry.

Key topics include:
- Teaching Kotlin fundamentals alongside the development of AI agents
- The new technical and problem-solving skills developers need to succeed in the AI era
- The limitations of traditional teaching methods and how interactive, AI-driven tools can enhance engagement
- The roles AI can play in programming education (e.g., automated feedback, AI code reviewers) and where human expertise remains critical

Attendees will leave with actionable insights and ready-to-use exercises for their own courses. Whether you’re an educator, curriculum designer, or industry instructor, this talk will empower you to prepare students for the challenges and opportunities of programming in the AI era.','{"id": "7b170dd75e74444d89d7c99a77076a3b", "room": "Room 3", "title": "Teaching Kotlin for the AI Era: Tips, Tools, and Practical Insights", "endsAt": 1779453900000, "category": "[Regular session, Introductory and overview, Language and best practices, AI, Other, Education]", "dayIndex": 2, "speakers": "[Anastasiia Birillo, Daniil Karol]", "startsAt": 1779451200000, "phaseOfDay": "AFTERNOON", "conferenceDay": "2026-05-22", "durationMinutes": 45, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-05-22T14:45:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-05-22T14:00:00"}');
