Using a zero-player simulation with each automaton signalling its own state-change event to the server, we''ll see how Exposed, a database access library, can assist with high throughput and the handling of asynchronous database operations. We''ll also leverage Kotlin Flow on top of Exposed DSL queries to observe a continuous data stream of all state updates to the UI.

At the end of the simulation cycle, we''ll jump into Kotlin Notebook, where we''ll retrieve our data using Exposed, then analyze and transform it using Kotlin DataFrame, and finally visualize the results using the Kandy plotting library.','{"id": "c91159655cde46b4ad6b2d432efb513e", "room": "Room 5, Lightning talks", "title": "Flow with Exposed: Life Finds a Way", "endsAt": 1779452100000, "category": "[Lightning talk, Intermediate, Server-side]", "dayIndex": 2, "speakers": "[Chantal Loncle]", "startsAt": 1779451200000, "phaseOfDay": "AFTERNOON", "conferenceDay": "2026-05-22", "durationMinutes": 15, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-05-22T14:15:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-05-22T14:00:00"}'),
