This migration was fraught with challenges, and required many enhancements to the Bazel ecosystem for Kotlin and Android. We invested heavily not only to make the migration possible at this scale, ship production apps, improve build performance, enhance the developer experience, unblock the latest Kotlin features, and preserve developer velocity throughout the transition.

This talk walks through the improvements across the entire ecosystem—ranging from modernization to performance optimizations, code-coverage integration, IDE experience improvements, as well as where things are going next.

Want to understand the state of Bazel for Android and Kotlin for your own needs, understand how to make it faster, or just curious how this works in production for large code-bases?  Don''t miss this talk.','{"id": "1f2e78b45c004bda89ebe9fa3b4fd1e7", "room": "Room 13a", "title": "Faster Kotlin with Bazel at Uber", "endsAt": 1779458400000, "category": "[Regular session, Intermediate, Android, Extensibility/Tooling]", "dayIndex": 2, "speakers": "[Ty Smith, Olivier Notteghem]", "startsAt": 1779455700000, "phaseOfDay": "AFTERNOON", "conferenceDay": "2026-05-22", "durationMinutes": 45, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-05-22T16:00:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-05-22T15:15:00"}'),
