In this talk, we’ll explore how JetBrains supports developer communities globally, with a special focus on Kotlin User Groups (KUGs), but also detailing the company’s work with GDGs and Java and Android user groups around the world. From local meetups to global initiatives, we’ll share how community leaders and JetBrains work together to create spaces where developers learn, connect, and grow.

You’ll learn how KUGs are started and sustained, what kinds of support JetBrains provides to organizers, and how community-driven initiatives help shape the future of the Kotlin ecosystem.

Whether you’re already running a meetup, thinking about starting a community, or simply curious about how one is built, this talk will offer practical insights and real-life stories from us.
