5,-0.028640747,-0.016052246,-0.0044822693,-0.018127441,0.016235352,-0.001282692,-0.0345459,-0.029266357,-0.0001745224,-0.0031280518,-0.022109985,0.016647339,-0.013450623,-0.007835388,0.003545761,0.04144287,0.049468994,0.0076141357,0.014350891,0.00024223328,0.00116539,-0.004573822,-0.026412964,-0.024902344,0.013336182,0.0036315918,0.04449463,0.012138367,0.002544403,-0.027267456,-0.022262573,0.013504028,-0.0010614395,-0.03338623,0.0035934448,-0.018234253,0.030670166,-0.0010643005,-0.0030269623,-0.027236938,0.03475952,-0.0070762634,-0.0044174194,-0.0017108917,0.012519836,0.040252686,0.002658844,-0.010650635,-0.004459381,0.02027893,-0.019882202,0.014198303,0.003293991,0.004146576,-0.01499939,0.016021729,-0.01335907,0.00048613548,-0.017028809,-0.001499176,0.0002732277,-0.0061531067,-0.021270752,-0.039489746,0.013183594,-0.020874023,0.04562378,-0.00983429,0.020187378,-0.0067367554,0.025482178,-0.007286072,0.011230469,-0.0178833,0.015129089,0.007522583,0.009391785,-0.0039901733,-0.016357422,-0.014335632,0.02444458,-0.03137207,-0.019088745,0.0031852722,0.02017212,-0.013259888,0.038024902,0.02520752,-0.014411926,0.020339966,0.012214661,-0.012969971,-0.01676941,-0.0014352798,0.0016765594,-0.023284912,-0.022384644,0.0037899017,0.0042915344,-0.00038170815,-0.025314331,0.044921875,-0.0256958,0.020401001,0.019958496,-0.015304565,-0.004184723,-0.02923584,-0.018814087,-0.017868042]'::public.vector,'title:Moments When Things Go Wrong, description:Sometimes you find yourself with a bug in a library or a tool you are using causing things to fail or even worse fail flakily. This talk will be a guide on how to take it from there. We''ll walk through examples of non-determinism, race-conditions, undocumented behavior and others to see what we can learn to make the process to a working build/application faster. We''ll look into an example of a race condition in the Kotlin Gradle Plugin. We''ll hone our skills in investigation, isolation of the issue to create a standalone reproduction, and finally getting it resolved. We''ll discuss at what point you should care about a problem or simply leave it alone. The stories will be inspired by Aurimas'' work on AndroidX libraries.','{"id": "1953e699d1334c5bb541ee9375b7e151", "room": "Auditorium, Room 1", "title": "Moments When Things Go Wrong", "endsAt": 1779462000000, "category": "[Regular session, Intermediate, Extensibility/Tooling, Other]", "dayIndex": 2, "speakers": "[Aurimas Liutikas]", "startsAt": 1779459300000, "phaseOfDay": "AFTERNOON", "conferenceDay": "2026-05-22", "durationMinutes": 45, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-05-22T17:00:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-05-22T16:15:00"}'),
